# Twilight terminator on terrain: one place, one heading, Sun swept from just above the
# horizon down to full night. The ground here must keep its ALBEDO and its sky-lighting
# all through civil twilight (Sun 0 .. -6 deg) and only hand over to the city-lights
# emissive look once the sky is actually dark; the sunlit peaks must stay red-orange
# throughout. Also captures the raw day albedo (debugview albedo) so the two can be told
# apart: a neutral-grey ground in the beauty frame while albedo shows biome colour = the
# ground is being painted by the night map.
#
# Alaska Peninsula (Veniaminof), looking east along the coast at 450 m AGL.
# Run before and after a terrain-lighting change, then imgtools stats/diff/sheet.
preset High
set clouds.coverage 0
set clouds.fog_coverage 0
observer lat=56.1 lon=-159.6 agl=450
camera az=90 el=3 fov=60

# The original repro instant: Sun 0.96 deg BELOW the horizon (bright civil twilight).
time set 2026-11-21T21:04:50Z
time pause
wait settle
capture tw_sun_m1

debugview albedo
wait settle
capture tw_sun_m1_albedo
debugview off

time sun 0 setting
wait settle
capture tw_sun_0

time sun -3 setting
wait settle
capture tw_sun_m3

time sun -6 setting
wait settle
capture tw_sun_m6

time sun -15 setting
wait settle
capture tw_sun_m15

perf frames=20 name=twilight_last
